<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Psekups</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Psekups is a river of the North-West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, a left tributary of the Kuban, flowing north from the Caucasus foothills through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Krasnodar</a> Krai and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adygea">Adygea</a>. The spa town of Goryachy Klyuch stands on its banks. Its valley was home to Circassian communities such as the Bzhedugh and Abadzekhs until the Russian conquest of the 1860s.</p></div>
